Six keyword spotters and digit transcribers, resolvable by `--model kws_<arch>`

ModelBlaster resolves --model <id> by importing modelblaster.models.<id>, so a model that
lives outside this submodule still needs a module inside it. These six are that module
and nothing else: each is ~20 lines that put $IISWC_ROOT on sys.path and defer to
fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/kws/mb_shim.py.

The architectures, the trained weights and the calibration clips deliberately stay in the
iiswc-tutorial repo rather than here:

  * this submodule is a PINNED READ-ONLY input -- scripts/02_verify_patches.sh proves the
    working tree equals its base plus patches/, and an untracked model file would pass
    that gate while not surviving a fresh checkout;
  * the trained weights are up to 560 KB of npz, which cannot be carried in a patch.

That is the same split patches/0009 uses for the curated MBP kernels, which live in
fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/kernels/ and reach the pipeline through --global-curated-dir.

The models, all on 10-coefficient MFCC from fpga/pynq-z2/sw/audio_fe.c:

  kws_cnn            2,729,728 MACs   dense conv, 12-class Speech Commands
  kws_dscnn          2,656,768 MACs   the MLPerf Tiny DS-CNN-S shape
  kws_cnn_tiny         679,616 MACs   a quarter of the budget
  kws_digit_ctc      2,067,200 MACs   connected-digit CTC transcriber
  kws_digit_ctc_wide 7,718,400 MACs   the same, wider
  kws_digit_ctc_t    7,718,400 MACs   the same again with time on the WIDTH axis, which
                                      is worth ~4x on this ISA for identical arithmetic

The last two are TRANSCRIBERS rather than classifiers: variable-length digit strings
decoded with CTC and scored with edit distance. Their graphs are conv2d_s8 and nothing
else, which is the whole reason they run here -- see fpga/pynq-z2/docs/SPEECH_ON_ROCKET.md
sections 11 and 12.

diff --git a/models/kws_cnn.py b/models/kws_cnn.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..51b6812
--- /dev/null
+++ b/models/kws_cnn.py
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+"""Keyword spotter 'cnn' -- see fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/kws/ in the iiswc-tutorial repo.
+
+Installed by patches/0020-modelblaster-kws-models.patch.  The architecture, the trained
+weights and the calibration clips live outside this submodule on purpose: the submodule
+is a pinned read-only input and a weight blob cannot be carried in a patch.
+"""
+import os
+import pathlib
+import sys
+
+_ROOT = pathlib.Path(os.environ.get("IISWC_ROOT", "/nonexistent"))
+sys.path.insert(0, str(_ROOT / "fpga" / "pynq-z2" / "modelblaster" / "kws"))
+import mb_shim  # noqa: E402
+
+_ARCH = "cnn"
+
+
+def get_model(seed: int = 0):
+    return mb_shim.load(_ARCH)[0]
+
+
+def get_sample_input(seed: int = 1):
+    return mb_shim.calib(_ARCH, 1)[0]
+
+
+def get_calibration_samples(n: int):
+    return mb_shim.calib(_ARCH, n)
